(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "etzhayyim is not designed or implemented as an ASI (Artificial Superintelligence) system, and its architecture deliberately avoids the monolithic-autonomous-agent / unbounded-recursive-self-improvement pattern"
                           "kotoba language does not currently satisfy the conditions needed to be \"a language for ASI\" — formal verification, runtime capability revocation, and sandboxed self-modification are all absent, and the language itself is pre-1.0"
                           "reference framework for this assessment is DeepMind \"From AGI to ASI\" (arXiv:2606.12683, 2026-06), not the 2024 \"Levels of AGI\" discrete-level taxonomy, which that later paper explicitly declines to reuse"
                           "this ADR is a standing factual assessment, not a decision to pursue ASI-readiness work — closing the formal-verification / capability-revocation / self-mod-sandbox gaps in kotoba is out of scope here and requires its own dedicated ADR if the owner chooses to pursue it"))
  (:adr/topic "asi-readiness-assessment-etzhayyim-kotoba-agi-to-asi-paper")
